# Auto-commit

The user asked for an automatic commit every time the project is modified.

At the end of every task that changes files in this repo:

1. Check `git status --short` and stage only the files you changed for that task (`git add <paths>`).
   Never stage `.pio/`, build outputs, captures, temporary harnesses or anything that looks like a secret.
2. Commit with a Conventional Commits message in English, matching the history:
   `feat(scope): ...`, `fix(scope): ...`, `docs: ...`, `refactor(scope): ...`, `chore: ...`.
   Add a short body when the subject is not enough. One commit per logical change.
3. Push to `origin main` (`git push origin main`).
4. Tell the user, in Spanish, the commit hash and message.

Do not commit if the build or the tests you ran for that change are failing; tell the user instead.
Do not amend or force-push existing commits.
